If the partial pressure of nitrogen at 293 K is 2.0 bar, how many moles of N_{2} will dissolve in 1 L of water? (K_{H} = 76.48 kbar)
x = p / K_{H} = 2.0 / (76.48 × 10^{3}) = 2.6 × 10^{−5}
1 L of water contains about 55.5 mol of water, and x is very small; so n ≈ x × 55.5 = **1.45 × 10^{−3} mol** (≈ 1.45 mmol).

p_{total} = p_{1} + p_{2} = x_{1} p_{1}° + x_{2} p_{2}°
    = p_{1}° + (p_{2}° − p_{1}°) x_{2}
In the vapour phase the mole fraction of component i is y_{i} = p_{i} / p_{total}
